 34P     208PB(36S,XG):XUNDL-9         2019GR08                           202003
 34P  c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2019Gr08:                          
 34P 2c  Phys Rev C 100, 064308 (2019)                                          
 34P  c  Compiled by B. Singh (McMaster), December 31, 2019                     
 34P  c  2019Gr08: E({+36}S)=225 MeV beam was provided by Tandem-ALPI           
 34P 2c  accelerator complex at the INFN Legnaro National Laboratory.           
 34P 4c  Target was 99.7% enriched in {+208}Pb with a thickness of 1 mg/cm{+2}  
 34P 5c  deposited on 1 mg/cm{+2} Nb backing, and mounted onto Cologne          
 34P 6c  differential plunger. Recoiling projectile-like fragments were         
 34P 7c  separated and identified by the PRISMA magnetic spectrometer.          
 34P 8c  The |g rays were detected with the AGATA demonstrator array of         
 34P 9c  five triple cluster modules of 36-fold segmented Ge crystals           
 34P Ac  at a distance of 18 cm from the reaction target position, covering     
 34P Bc  backward angles 135|' to 175|'. Measured E|g, ({+34}P)|g-coin, and     
 34P Cc  and level lifetime using differential recoil-distance method.          
 34P Dc  Comparison with shell-model calculations using PSDPF effective         
 34P Ec  interaction.                                                           
 34P  c  Level scheme is from a previous paper by                               
 34P 2c  the same experimental group: 2015Ch56: Phys. Rev. C 92, 044308 (2015). 
 34P 3c  Note that detailed level schemes are also available from 2012Be11      
 34P 4c  (Phys. Rev. C 85, 044305) and 2018Lu08 (Phys. Rev. C 97, 044312).      
